From 3bd07986c756f94d3fd49c12b54388abcdc76d91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: give Bluetooth back its
 uart

Bluetooth stopped working on this board when it moved to megi's 7.2 tree,
and uart1 is why.

The BES2600 is a combo part: WiFi rides the SDIO bus, Bluetooth speaks HCI
over uart1, and userspace attaches it with

    hciattach -s 1500000 /dev/ttyS1 any 1500000 flow nosleep

so that port has to be a full bidirectional UART with hardware flow
control.  The LuneOS 6.6 device tree described exactly that.

Commit 5f8520766526 ("arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3566-pinetab2: Add DT nodes
for besdbg driver") repurposed the same port as a one-way serial console
for reading the BES2600's debug output, and overrode the pinmux to match:

    <2 RK_PB3 2 &pcfg_pull_down>,              // RX
    <2 RK_PB4 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_down>;   // TX

RX stays on uart function 2, but TX is parked on GPIO, and CTS and RTS are
never muxed at all -- uart1m0_ctsn and uart1m0_rtsn are /omit-if-no-ref/,
so with nothing referencing them they are dropped from the DTB entirely.
That is a perfectly good debug console and it is still doing its job: the
chip's "[bt_time] execute main" banner arrives over RX.  It cannot carry
HCI, because the SoC has no way to transmit.

The symptom is easy to misread.  hci0 appears, hciattach reports success,
and every command then times out at -110 with an all-zero BD address, which
all points at the controller or its firmware.  Both are fine -- the counters
give it away: TX bytes climb with each attempt while RX bytes stay at 0.
Passing "noflow" does not help either, since that only relaxes the host's
termios and cannot mux a pin.

So put the port back the way the driver needs it: stock uart1m0_xfer has
both pins on function 2, and referencing the ctsn and rtsn groups brings
them into the DTB so uart-has-rtscts has something to drive.

The debug console keeps working; RX is unchanged apart from the pull, which
returns to the pull-up the stock definition uses.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific: mainline has no Bluetooth
node for this board, and megi's tree wants the port as a debug console]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts
index 530961ed2a35..58f3b68ddf46 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2-v2.0.dts
@@ -142,15 +142,19 @@ bes2600: wifi@1 {
 	};
 };
 
-// for wifi chip comm
+// BES2600 Bluetooth: HCI over uart1 with hardware flow control, plus the
+// chip's debug console on the same port.
 &uart1 {
-	pinctrl-0 = <&uart1m0_xfer>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&uart1m0_xfer>, <&uart1m0_ctsn>, <&uart1m0_rtsn>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	uart-has-rtscts;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+// Stock rk3568 muxing: both pins on uart function 2.  megi's besdbg change
+// parked TX on GPIO, which left the port unable to transmit.
 &uart1m0_xfer {
 	rockchip,pins =
-		<2 RK_PB3 2 &pcfg_pull_down>, // RX
-		<2 RK_PB4 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_down>; // TX
+		<2 RK_PB3 2 &pcfg_pull_up>, // RX
+		<2 RK_PB4 2 &pcfg_pull_up>; // TX
 };
